# Workflow Standards

Thin hub: domain detail lives in the linked rules and docs. Never re-grow this file with domain bodies — add a sibling `.claude/rules/<category>.md` and one row below.

## Where things live (SSOT)

| Concern | SSOT |
|---------|------|
| Branch model, PRs, production, commit timing | `.claude/rules/git-workflow.md` § Mode behavior table (mode: `src/config/git-workflow.json`) |
| Semver, changelog, commit format | same table → **version source** (A/B: `.agents/skills/finish/SKILL.md`; C: release-please) |
| Protected files, decision protocol, success reporting | `.claude/rules/agent-behavior.md` |
| Shell rules, env vars | `.agents/skills/platform/SKILL.md` |
| Architecture, code placement | `.claude/rules/architecture.md`; whitelist `projectStructure.config.cjs`; layers `.dependency-cruiser.cjs` |
| Reductive strategy, debugging | `.claude/rules/debugging.md` |
| API / vendor research | `.claude/rules/api-integration.md` |
| Dev task backlog / onboarding | `src/config/app-tasks.json` + `src/features/tasks/README.md` |
| App vision | `documentation/DOC_APP_VISION.md` |
| Agent workflow layers | `documentation/DOC_AGENT_WORKFLOW_LAYERS.md` |
| Frontend hosting (Cloudflare Workers) | `documentation/DOC_CLOUDFLARE_WORKERS.md` + `wrangler.jsonc` |
| Edge / cloud functions deploys | `.claude/rules/cloud-functions.md` |

## Branch gate

Read `src/config/git-workflow.json`, then apply `.claude/rules/git-workflow.md` § Mode-aware branch gate. Do not infer the mode from the current branch.

## During development

- **Agents:** commit only per the table's **commit timing** row (A/B: only in `finish`, never during `plan`/`implement`; C: when the user asks, directly or via `finish`). Humans may commit freely on the branch their mode allows.
- Write tests per `.claude/rules/testing.md` § When to use TDD / What to test and how.
- Deploy functions yourself when a change requires it, and verify the deploy succeeded.

## Before handing off / review checklist

- [ ] Version + changelog per the **version source** row (A/B: `[VERSION]`-first commit via `finish`; C: conventional PR title)
- [ ] `code-style`, `architecture`, `testing`, `security` rules followed; lint, type-check, tests pass
- [ ] Only required docs touched: `ARCHITECTURE.md` (structural changes), `src/features/*/README.md` (staged with feature code), `CHANGELOG.md` when the version-source row says `finish`. New deep docs need explicit user approval.
- [ ] No leftover debug code (but keep debugging logs until the user confirms — `.claude/rules/debugging.md`)

## Related Rules

When modifying this rule, check `git-workflow`, `agent-behavior`, `platform`, `code-style`, `architecture`, `testing`, `security`, `cloud-functions`, and `api-integration`.
